#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"In Qiskit, quantum operators are represented using classes from the [`quantum_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/quantum_info) module. The most important operator class is [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp), which represents a general quantum operator as a linear combination of Pauli strings. `SparsePauliOp` is the class most commonly used to represent quantum observables. The rest of this page explains how to use `SparsePauliOp` and other operator classes.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Dalam Qiskit, operator kuantum diwakili menggunakan kelas daripada modul [`quantum_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/quantum_info). Kelas operator yang paling penting ialah [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp), yang mewakili operator kuantum umum sebagai gabungan linear rentetan Pauli. `SparsePauliOp` adalah kelas yang paling kerap digunakan untuk mewakili observable kuantum. Selebihnya halaman ini menerangkan cara menggunakan `SparsePauliOp` dan kelas operator lain.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "SparsePauliOp {#sparsepauliop}"
msgstr "SparsePauliOp {#sparsepauliop}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) class represents a linear combination of Pauli strings. There are several ways to initialize a `SparsePauliOp`, but the most flexible way is to use the [`from_sparse_list`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_sparse_list) method, as demonstrated in the following code cell. The `from_sparse_list` accepts a list of `(pauli_string, qubit_indices, coefficient)` triplets.\n"
msgstr "Kelas [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) mewakili gabungan linear rentetan Pauli. Terdapat beberapa cara untuk memulakan `SparsePauliOp`, tetapi cara yang paling fleksibel ialah menggunakan kaedah [`from_sparse_list`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_sparse_list), seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam sel kod berikut. `from_sparse_list` menerima senarai triplet `(pauli_string, qubit_indices, coefficient)`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`SparsePauliOp` supports arithmetic operations, as demonstrated in the following code cell.\n"
msgstr "`SparsePauliOp` menyokong operasi aritmetik, seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam sel kod berikut.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli {#pauli}"
msgstr "Pauli {#pauli}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`Pauli`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Pauli) class represents a single Pauli string with an optional phase coefficient from the set $\\set{+1, i, -1, -i}$. A `Pauli` can be initialized by passing a string of characters from the set `{\"I\", \"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}`, optionally prefixed by one of `{\"\", \"i\", \"-\", \"-i\"}` to represent the phase coefficient.\n"
msgstr "Kelas [`Pauli`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Pauli) mewakili satu rentetan Pauli dengan pekali fasa pilihan daripada set $\\set{+1, i, -1, -i}$. `Pauli` boleh dimulakan dengan menghantar rentetan aksara daripada set `{\"I\", \"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"}`, secara pilihan diawali oleh salah satu daripada `{\"\", \"i\", \"-\", \"-i\"}` untuk mewakili pekali fasa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code cell demonstrates the use of some attributes and methods.\n"
msgstr "Sel kod berikut menunjukkan penggunaan beberapa atribut dan kaedah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Pauli` objects possess a number of other methods to manipulate the operators such as determining its adjoint, whether it (anti)commutes with another `Pauli`, and computing the dot product with another `Pauli`. Refer to the [API documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Pauli) for more info.\n"
msgstr "Objek `Pauli` mempunyai pelbagai kaedah lain untuk memanipulasi operator, seperti menentukan adjointnya, sama ada ia (anti)komut dengan `Pauli` lain, dan mengira hasil darab titik dengan `Pauli` lain. Rujuk [dokumentasi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Pauli) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operator {#operator}"
msgstr "Operator {#operator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) class represents a general linear operator. Unlike `SparsePauliOp`, `Operator` stores the linear operator as a dense matrix. Because the memory required to store a dense matrix scales exponentially with the number of qubits, the `Operator` class is only suitable for use with a small number of qubits.\n"
msgstr "Kelas [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) mewakili operator linear umum. Berbeza dengan `SparsePauliOp`, `Operator` menyimpan operator linear sebagai matriks padat. Oleh sebab memori yang diperlukan untuk menyimpan matriks padat meningkat secara eksponen mengikut bilangan qubit, kelas `Operator` hanya sesuai digunakan dengan bilangan qubit yang kecil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can initialize an `Operator` by directly passing a Numpy array storing the matrix of the operator. For example, the following code cell creates a two-qubit Pauli XX operator:\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh memulakan `Operator` dengan menghantar terus tatasusunan Numpy yang menyimpan matriks operator. Contohnya, sel kod berikut mencipta operator Pauli XX dua-Qubit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator object stores the underlying matrix, and the input and output dimension of subsystems.\n"
msgstr "Objek operator menyimpan matriks asas, serta dimensi input dan output subsistem.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`data`: To access the underlying Numpy array, you can use the `Operator.data` property.\n"
msgstr "`data`: Untuk mengakses tatasusunan Numpy asas, anda boleh menggunakan sifat `Operator.data`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`dims`: To return the total input and output dimension of the operator, you can use the `Operator.dim` property. *Note: the output is returned as a tuple* `(input_dim, output_dim)`, *which is the reverse of the shape of the underlying matrix.*\n"
msgstr "`dims`: Untuk mendapatkan jumlah dimensi input dan output operator, anda boleh menggunakan sifat `Operator.dim`. *Nota: output dikembalikan sebagai tuple* `(input_dim, output_dim)`, *yang merupakan songsangan bentuk matriks asas.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator class also keeps track of subsystem dimensions, which can be used for composing operators together. These can be accessed using the `input_dims` and `output_dims` functions.\n"
msgstr "Kelas operator juga menjejak dimensi subsistem, yang boleh digunakan untuk menggabungkan operator bersama-sama. Ini boleh diakses menggunakan fungsi `input_dims` dan `output_dims`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For $2^N$ by $2^M$ operators, the input and output dimensions are automatically assumed to be M-qubit and N-qubit:\n"
msgstr "Untuk operator $2^N$ kali $2^M$, dimensi input dan output secara automatik dianggap sebagai M-Qubit dan N-Qubit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the input matrix is not divisible into qubit subsystems, then it will be stored as a single-qubit operator. For example, for a $6\\times6$ matrix:\n"
msgstr "Jika matriks input tidak boleh dibahagikan kepada subsistem qubit, ia akan disimpan sebagai operator satu-Qubit. Contohnya, untuk matriks $6\\times6$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The input and output dimension can also be manually specified when initializing a new operator:\n"
msgstr "Dimensi input dan output juga boleh ditentukan secara manual semasa memulakan operator baharu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also extract just the input or output dimensions of a subset of subsystems using the `input_dims` and `output_dims` functions:\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh mengekstrak hanya dimensi input atau output subset subsistem menggunakan fungsi `input_dims` dan `output_dims`:\n"

